window.RTBO_CONTRACT_LIBRARY = {"name":"RTBO Contract Library","version":"1.1","date":"August 10, 2026","archiveUrl":"library/Contracts.zip","documentCount":31,"templateCount":30,"items":[{"key":"library-00-contract-library-guide","code":"00","title":"CONTRACT LIBRARY GUIDE","documentTitle":"CONTRACT LIBRARY GUIDE","subtitle":"Arkansas-First Standalone Templates | Version 1.0 | August 3, 2026","category":"Library Guide","primaryUse":"Completion, classification, public-entity, safety, data, screening, insurance, execution, and legal-review guidance for the full RTBO contract library.","filename":"00_RTBO_Contract_Library_Guide.docx","url":"library/docx/00_RTBO_Contract_Library_Guide.docx","isGuide":true,"preamble":"This library was prepared for Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. to support assigning, officiating, training, events, education, sponsorships, vendors, customers, venues, data handling, evaluators, public entities, participants, media, employment, and background screening. The forms are written as standalone agreements: each contains its own core commercial, compliance, risk, termination, dispute, and signature terms, plus a fillable Schedule 1.","clauses":[],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. These are sophisticated editable templates, not a guarantee of enforceability or universal legal compliance. No single form can satisfy every jurisdiction, sport, public entity, worker relationship, event, or fact pattern. A licensed attorney must review the completed agreement, referenced policies, insurance, and actual operating practices before execution.","tables":[[["Document","Primary Use"],["01 Officials Service Agreement","Independent officials accepting discrete assignments."],["02 School Services Agreement","Private or public school, district, college, or university services."],["03 Program Services Agreement","Athletic, educational, youth, recreation, or development programs."],["04 Training School Agreement","Clinics, camps, seminars, live-game training, and evaluation schools."],["05 Sponsor Agreement","Cash or in-kind sponsorship and activation."],["06 Vendor Services Agreement","Goods, services, technology, production, logistics, and vendors."],["07 Independent Contractor Agreement","Non-official contractors when classification facts support it."],["08 Customer Agreement","Business or consumer purchases, registrations, subscriptions, or services."],["09 Master Officiating and Assigning Services Agreement","Recurring or multi-season client relationships with statements of work."],["10 League and Conference Assigning Agreement","Centralized assigning for leagues, conferences, districts, or associations."],["11 Tournament / Showcase / Special Event Agreement","Compressed, multi-court, or special-event officiating."],["12 Official Assignment Acceptance","A specific game or event confirmation."],["13 Venue and Facility Use Agreement","Gyms, classrooms, courts, meeting, and event spaces."],["14 Data Privacy, Confidentiality, and Security Agreement","Protected personal, student, assignment, evaluation, and system data."],["15 Mutual Nondisclosure Agreement","Precontract or project confidentiality."],["16 Evaluator, Observer, and Training Personnel Agreement","Evaluators, clinicians, trainers, mentors, and observers."],["17 Governmental and Public Entity Services Agreement","Public schools, universities, municipalities, and government bodies."],["18 Participant Enrollment / Risk / Medical Authorization","Participant and parent/guardian enrollment and emergency authorization."],["19 Media Recording and Publicity Release","Choice-based image, video, audio, and publicity permission."],["20 Sports Official Employment Agreement","Use when facts or law require employee treatment."],["21A-21D FCRA Forms","Separate disclosure, authorization, pre-adverse, and final adverse notices."]]],"paragraphCount":50,"fileSize":419232,"sha256":"a180a8f3ef2b6455534ef9c3a2f925257adadd7e50686ac7fd5595c6693c41ba"},{"key":"library-01-officials-service-agreement","code":"01","title":"OFFICIALS SERVICE AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"OFFICIALS SERVICE AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Officials and Assignments","primaryUse":"Independent officials accepting discrete assignments.","filename":"01_Officials_Service_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/01_Officials_Service_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Officials Service Agreement is entered into by Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the individual identified as Official. RTBO engages Official to accept and perform discrete sports-officiating assignments under the terms below, and Official accepts that engagement.","clauses":[{"title":"Engagement and Assignment-by-Assignment Structure","body":"RTBO may offer games, events, evaluations, camps, clinics, or related officiating assignments. Official may accept or decline each offer before acceptance. No minimum volume, exclusivity, or continuing assignment is promised. A confirmed assignment becomes binding when accepted through the approved platform, writing, or other documented method."},{"title":"Officiating Standards and Authority","body":"Official shall arrive on time, properly equipped and attired; hold all credentials listed in Schedule 1; know and apply the designated rules and mechanics; exercise independent judgment on play rulings; communicate professionally; complete required reports; avoid gambling and conflicts; and follow lawful safety, conduct, antiharassment, and venue procedures. No party may require alteration of an on-court ruling for an improper purpose."},{"title":"Assignment Changes; Substitution; No-Shows","body":"Official shall not transfer or subcontract an assignment without RTBO approval. If unavailable after acceptance, Official must notify RTBO immediately and reasonably assist with replacement, but only RTBO or the authorized assignor may confirm a substitute. Unexcused lateness, abandonment, or no-show may result in removal, documented losses, and discipline consistent with published policy and law."},{"title":"Compensation and Payment Administration","body":"Official earns only the fee and approved expenses for completed or compensable cancelled assignments shown in the assignment confirmation. RTBO may administer payment for a client but does not guarantee client funds unless Schedule 1 expressly makes RTBO the primary payor. Deductions or offsets require a lawful, documented basis and notice."},{"title":"Independent Business Status","body":"Official represents that Official is independently engaged in officiating or related services, may serve other assignors and organizations, controls lawful means and methods of performance except for results, safety, rules, and event requirements, supplies ordinary personal equipment, bears ordinary business expenses, and is responsible for taxes and benefits. This clause does not override governing law or actual facts; the parties will amend the relationship or use employment documentation if required."},{"title":"Credentials; Fitness; Background Information","body":"Official shall maintain required registrations, training, rules examinations, physical ability, background-screening eligibility, driving status when applicable, and accurate profile and tax information. Official shall promptly report any suspension, disqualification, charge, conviction, restraining order, or other fact legally relevant to safety, trust, eligibility, or assignment suitability, subject to applicable fair-chance and privacy laws."},{"title":"Incident and Injury Reporting","body":"Official shall promptly report serious injury, ejection, fight, threat, harassment, discrimination, security failure, suspected abuse, unusual game termination, or other reportable incident through RTBO’s approved process, while preserving evidence and protecting confidential information."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Use this form only when the actual relationship supports independent-contractor classification. Scheduling practices, control, economic dependence, exclusivity, equipment, tax treatment, and the parties’ day-to-day conduct must match the agreement. Use the separate Sports Official Employment Agreement when the facts support employee status.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Official","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Sport / Governing Rules","[SPORT; NFHS/NCAA/NAIA/NJCAA/FIBA/LEAGUE RULES]"],["Credentials Required","[REGISTRATION, CERTIFICATION, TRAINING, BACKGROUND SCREEN]"],["Assignment Offer / Acceptance Method","[PLATFORM / EMAIL / WRITTEN CONFIRMATION]"],["Standard Game Fees","[BY LEVEL, POSITION, OR EVENT]"],["Payment Timing","[NUMBER] days after [COMPLETED GAME / CLIENT FUNDING / APPROVED INVOICE]"],["Travel / Expenses","[MILEAGE, LODGING, PER DIEM, PARKING]"],["Cancellation / Postponement Fees","[TERMS]"],["Uniform / Equipment","[REQUIRED ITEMS AND RESPONSIBILITY]"],["Reporting Deadlines","[GAME / INCIDENT / EJECTION REPORTS]"],["Insurance Requirements","[IF ANY]"],["Tax Forms","Form W-9 and other legally required information"],["Term / Convenience Termination","[TERM]; [NUMBER] days notice"],["Notices","RTBO: [ADDRESS/EMAIL] | Official: [ADDRESS/EMAIL]"],["Special Terms","[ADDITIONAL TERMS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","OFFICIAL"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":47,"fileSize":420580,"sha256":"b9fd8a0bfa3cfff95e10c6c43af4062d19957a4ac827573dbca9ab2c25150101"},{"key":"library-02-school-services-agreement","code":"02","title":"SCHOOL SERVICES AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"SCHOOL SERVICES AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Schools and Programs","primaryUse":"Private or public school, district, college, or university services.","filename":"02_School_Services_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/02_School_Services_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This School Services Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified school, district, college, university, or educational institution for officiating, assigning, training, evaluation, consulting, event-support, or related services.","clauses":[{"title":"Services and Service Orders","body":"RTBO shall provide only the services stated in Schedule 1 or a signed service order, which may include recruiting and assigning officials, schedule administration, game coverage, replacement coordination, training, evaluations, reports, payment administration, or consulting. A service order must identify sport, level, dates, facilities, staffing model, deliverables, fees, and authorized contacts."},{"title":"School Responsibilities","body":"School shall provide accurate schedules and changes; safe, regulation-compliant facilities; site administration and security; participant and spectator control; emergency and medical plans; secure dressing space where required; parking and access; timely payment; and a person authorized to resolve operational issues. School retains responsibility for students, athletes, coaches, spectators, employees, facilities, and institutional compliance."},{"title":"Assignment Independence and Noninterference","body":"RTBO controls the assignment process within governing-body rules and disclosed conflict standards. School may identify legitimate eligibility, safety, credential, or conflict concerns but may not demand discriminatory assignments, retaliate against officials, manipulate evaluations, or interfere with good-faith rulings. RTBO may replace personnel when operationally reasonable."},{"title":"Schedule Changes; Minimum Coverage; Cancellations","body":"School shall deliver schedules and changes through the designated system. Late changes, added contests, venue changes, postponements, cancellations, or failures to provide access may trigger minimum, cancellation, travel, or replacement fees in Schedule 1. RTBO will use commercially reasonable efforts to cover changes but does not warrant coverage when notice is inadequate or qualified personnel are unavailable."},{"title":"Student Records and Institutional Data","body":"The parties shall identify whether RTBO will receive education records or other protected student information. Unless Schedule 1 expressly authorizes access, School shall not disclose education records. If authorized, RTBO will act only within the written scope, under School’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, and only for legitimate institutional interests."},{"title":"Athletic Risk Allocation","body":"RTBO is responsible for its contracted services and personnel as provided by law. School remains responsible for premises, crowd management, emergency response, participant eligibility, coaching, medical care, and institutional acts or omissions. Officiating judgment does not transfer ownership or operational control of the event to RTBO."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Governmental Limitations; No Waiver","body":"Nothing requires a public entity to indemnify, defend, insure, pay, or assume liability beyond authority granted by law or available appropriations, and nothing waives constitutional, statutory, sovereign, governmental, qualified, or other immunity. Any indemnity or liability obligation imposed on a public entity applies only to the extent lawfully authorized."},{"title":"Appropriation; Procurement; Audit; Public Records","body":"Payment obligations of a public entity are subject to lawful appropriation and available funds. The parties shall complete applicable bidding, purchasing, vendor-registration, conflict-disclosure, contract-review, and approval procedures. Records shall be maintained and made available for lawful audit. Materials may be subject to freedom-of-information or public-records laws; the receiving public entity will determine disclosure duties and, when legally permitted, provide notice before disclosing material marked confidential."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Public and private educational institutions have different procurement, appropriation, immunity, student-record, insurance, and approval requirements. The institution’s authorized legal and procurement representatives must review and complete this agreement before execution.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["School / Educational Institution","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Institution / Campus","[LEGAL NAME, CAMPUS, DISTRICT, SYSTEM]"],["Sport / Level / Governing Body","[DETAILS]"],["Services","[ASSIGNING, OFFICIATING, TRAINING, PAYMENT, EVALUATION]"],["Season / Event Dates","[DATES]"],["Facilities","[NAMES, ADDRESSES, SITE CONTACTS]"],["Crew Configuration","[2-PERSON / 3-PERSON / OTHER; ALTERNATE]"],["Fees","[ASSIGNING FEE; GAME FEES; ADMIN FEES; OTHER]"],["Payment Terms","[DEPOSIT, INVOICE SCHEDULE, DUE DATE]"],["Schedule Change Deadline","[METHOD AND DEADLINE]"],["Cancellation / Postponement","[TERMS]"],["Security / Medical / Site Duties","[SCHOOL RESPONSIBILITIES]"],["Student Data Access","[NONE / SPECIFIC AUTHORIZED DATA AND PURPOSE]"],["Insurance","[LIMITS AND CERTIFICATES]"],["Approvals / Purchase Order","[PO, BOARD, PROCUREMENT, LEGAL REVIEW]"],["Notices / Administrators","[CONTACTS]"],["Special Terms","[TERMS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","SCHOOL / EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTION"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":47,"fileSize":420363,"sha256":"d30687ec919621b6e1623a13c0d7cc8e83a73c299d925f13e00f25f947f080e1"},{"key":"library-03-program-services-agreement","code":"03","title":"PROGRAM SERVICES AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"PROGRAM SERVICES AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Schools and Programs","primaryUse":"Athletic, educational, youth, recreation, or development programs.","filename":"03_Program_Services_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/03_Program_Services_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Program Services Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified organization operating an athletic, educational, youth, recreational, community, or development program.","clauses":[{"title":"Program Scope and Deliverables","body":"RTBO shall provide the programming, staffing, officiating, assigning, training, evaluation, curriculum, administration, or consulting deliverables specifically listed in Schedule 1. Objectives, attendance limits, calendar, milestones, acceptance criteria, and reporting must be stated with enough detail to measure performance."},{"title":"Program Operator Duties","body":"Program Operator shall enroll eligible participants; obtain consents and medical information; provide safe facilities, equipment, supervision, security, and emergency plans; communicate rules; administer participant conduct; and assign a qualified on-site decision maker. RTBO does not assume custody of participants except to the limited extent expressly stated."},{"title":"Personnel and Screening","body":"Each party is responsible for selecting, training, supervising, and paying its personnel. Personnel who may interact with minors or vulnerable persons must complete legally and programmatically required screening and safeguarding before access. Screening decisions shall be made lawfully, individually when required, and through separate compliant disclosures and authorizations."},{"title":"Curriculum and Materials","body":"Unless Schedule 1 states otherwise, RTBO retains ownership of its curriculum, methods, videos, forms, and training assets and grants a limited, nontransferable license for enrolled participants during the program. Program Operator may not record, reproduce, resell, or create derivative materials without written permission."},{"title":"Participant Conduct, Removal, and Emergencies","body":"The parties shall enforce published conduct and safety rules. Either party may remove or suspend a participant or staff member for a reasonable safety, safeguarding, disruption, eligibility, or misconduct concern, subject to applicable law and any promised process. Emergency action takes priority over ordinary notice procedures."},{"title":"Fees, Enrollment, Refunds, and Scholarships","body":"Schedule 1 shall state whether fees are paid by Program Operator or participants, who processes payments, refund and transfer rules, scholarship authority, taxes, chargeback responsibility, and treatment of minimum enrollment. No refund term limits nonwaivable consumer rights."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Complete a separate schedule for each program. Youth programs require safeguarding, screening, parental-consent, medical, transportation, and mandatory-reporting procedures appropriate to the jurisdiction and governing body.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Program Operator","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Program Name / Purpose","[DETAILS]"],["Population / Eligibility / Capacity","[DETAILS]"],["Dates / Times / Locations","[DETAILS]"],["RTBO Deliverables","[STAFFING, OFFICIATING, CURRICULUM, REPORTS]"],["Program Operator Deliverables","[FACILITY, SUPERVISION, ENROLLMENT, SECURITY, MEDICAL]"],["Personnel / Ratios / Screening","[DETAILS]"],["Participant Forms / Policies","[LIST AND DEADLINES]"],["Fees / Payment Processor","[DETAILS]"],["Refund / Transfer / Scholarship Rules","[DETAILS]"],["Minimum Enrollment / Cancellation","[DETAILS]"],["Curriculum License / Materials","[DETAILS]"],["Data / Privacy / Media","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance","[DETAILS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Term / Termination","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","PROGRAM OPERATOR"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":420011,"sha256":"c49c2072c9c7bec7e50e906b25da24a950dec9d38ad6e9f8f60e2904ec6442eb"},{"key":"library-04-training-school-agreement","code":"04","title":"TRAINING SCHOOL AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"TRAINING SCHOOL AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Training and Education","primaryUse":"Clinics, camps, seminars, live-game training, and evaluation schools.","filename":"04_Training_School_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/04_Training_School_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Training School Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified host, school, institution, camp, league, facility, or training partner for an officiating school, clinic, camp, seminar, evaluation event, or professional-development program.","clauses":[{"title":"Training Event and Learning Services","body":"The training event, dates, curriculum, instructors, observer/evaluator model, on-court or live-game components, capacity, learning outcomes, materials, and certificates are described in Schedule 1. RTBO may make reasonable instructional changes that do not materially reduce the promised program."},{"title":"Host Responsibilities","body":"Host shall provide the facilities, game inventory, participants or teams, site access, classrooms, courts, audiovisual resources, score-table support, security, medical coverage, permits, housing or meals, and other items assigned to Host in Schedule 1. Host shall disclose known facility hazards and schedule changes promptly."},{"title":"RTBO Responsibilities","body":"RTBO shall provide the instructors, clinicians, evaluators, curriculum, assignments, student communications, registration support, materials, and reports allocated to RTBO. RTBO personnel shall meet stated credentials and conduct requirements."},{"title":"Evaluation and Certification Disclaimer","body":"Evaluations are professional opinions based on observed performance and identified criteria. Completion, scores, rankings, recommendations, or certificates do not guarantee employment, assignments, advancement, licensing, or selection by any third party. RTBO may correct clerical errors and investigate academic or conduct integrity concerns."},{"title":"Participant Documentation","body":"Before participation, responsible parties shall obtain enrollment terms, informed risk acknowledgment, medical and emergency authorization where appropriate, code of conduct, privacy notice, and media choice. Minors require legally sufficient parent or guardian execution. Forms shall be retained according to Schedule 1 and applicable law."},{"title":"Revenue, Expenses, and Reconciliation","body":"Schedule 1 shall state registration ownership, pricing authority, deposits, complimentary registrations, refunds, chargebacks, scholarships, taxes, vendor costs, revenue share, minimum guarantees, reconciliation timing, and audit support. Neither party may make unapproved financial commitments for the other."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. This agreement allocates host and training responsibilities but does not replace participant enrollment, assumption-of-risk, medical authorization, media release, staff, venue, or background-screening documents when those are needed.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Host / Training Partner","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Training School / Event","[NAME]"],["Dates / Locations / Facilities","[DETAILS]"],["Curriculum / Learning Outcomes","[DETAILS]"],["Live-Game / On-Court Components","[DETAILS]"],["Instructors / Evaluators / Credentials","[DETAILS]"],["Capacity / Eligibility / Prerequisites","[DETAILS]"],["RTBO Responsibilities","[DETAILS]"],["Host Responsibilities","[FACILITY, TEAMS, SECURITY, MEDICAL, A/V, ETC.]"],["Registration / Pricing / Processor","[DETAILS]"],["Deposits / Revenue Share / Reconciliation","[DETAILS]"],["Refund / Cancellation / Minimum Enrollment","[DETAILS]"],["Travel / Lodging / Meals","[DETAILS]"],["Participant Forms / Safeguarding","[DETAILS]"],["Evaluation / Certificate Standards","[DETAILS]"],["Materials / Recording / Data","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance / Permits","[DETAILS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","HOST / TRAINING PARTNER"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":420027,"sha256":"537dd7489d68ec9e44903ee8d69f0c7f9144ef2a1ede3def17cf0408d30946de"},{"key":"library-05-sponsor-agreement","code":"05","title":"SPONSOR AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"SPONSOR AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Sponsors and Customers","primaryUse":"Cash or in-kind sponsorship and activation.","filename":"05_Sponsor_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/05_Sponsor_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Sponsor Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Sponsor for cash or in-kind support in exchange for the specific recognition, activation, hospitality, content, or promotional benefits stated in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Sponsorship Rights and Benefits","body":"RTBO grants only the category, territory, term, inventory, impressions, placements, tickets, hospitality, speaking, content, digital, signage, naming, or activation benefits specifically identified in Schedule 1. Estimated reach is not guaranteed unless an express minimum and remedy are stated."},{"title":"Sponsorship Fee and In-Kind Value","body":"Sponsor shall pay the fee and deliver in-kind items according to Schedule 1. In-kind items require written valuation, delivery, acceptance, quality, warranty, and disposal terms. Taxes, permits, fulfillment, shipping, and activation expenses are allocated in Schedule 1."},{"title":"Approvals and Brand Standards","body":"Each party must approve the other’s proposed use of its name, logo, marks, claims, and creative materials before publication. Approval does not shift responsibility for accuracy or legal compliance. Materials must comply with school, governing-body, platform, advertising, endorsement, accessibility, intellectual-property, and privacy requirements."},{"title":"Category Exclusivity and Conflicts","body":"Any exclusivity is limited to the exact category, event, media, territory, and term in Schedule 1. RTBO may maintain existing relationships and accept nonconflicting sponsors. Sponsor shall disclose conflicts, prohibited relationships, sanctions, and reputational risks. No arrangement may compromise competitive integrity or create an improper inducement."},{"title":"Content; Publicity; Talent and Participant Rights","body":"No individual’s name, image, likeness, voice, testimonial, student information, or endorsement may be used without required permission. Sponsor is responsible for substantiating product claims and required disclosures. Alcohol, gambling, tobacco, cannabis, weapons, adult, political, and other sensitive categories require RTBO’s express written approval and may be prohibited."},{"title":"Makegoods and Cancellation","body":"If a material sponsored benefit cannot be delivered, RTBO may provide a reasonably equivalent makegood, prorated credit, or refund as specified in Schedule 1. Sponsor has no remedy for changes required by law, safety, governing-body rule, or force majeure beyond the negotiated makegood or refund provisions."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Sponsorship does not grant control over officiating assignments, rulings, evaluations, eligibility, discipline, educational content, or safety decisions. Regulated products and school-related sponsorships require special legal and policy review.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Sponsor","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Sponsored Program / Event","[NAME AND DATES]"],["Sponsorship Level / Category","[DETAILS]"],["Territory / Exclusivity","[EXACT CATEGORY, MEDIA, TERRITORY, TERM]"],["Cash Sponsorship Fee","[AMOUNT AND PAYMENT SCHEDULE]"],["In-Kind Contribution / Value","[ITEMS, DELIVERY, ACCEPTANCE, VALUE]"],["Recognition / Signage / Naming","[INVENTORY AND SPECIFICATIONS]"],["Digital / Content / Social Benefits","[CHANNELS, POSTS, PLACEMENTS]"],["Hospitality / Tickets / Activation","[DETAILS]"],["Creative Submission / Approval Deadlines","[DETAILS]"],["Marks / Brand Guidelines","[DETAILS]"],["Talent / Participant / Endorsement Rights","[DETAILS OR NONE]"],["Estimated Reach / Guaranteed Minimums","[DETAILS OR NONE]"],["Makegoods / Credits / Refunds","[DETAILS]"],["Sensitive-Category Restrictions","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance / Permits / Taxes","[DETAILS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","SPONSOR"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":41,"fileSize":419517,"sha256":"02d843d3ff6ee0f34998e4b93ede7784a22b9b337680d5aecc02e913e341eee9"},{"key":"library-06-vendor-services-agreement","code":"06","title":"VENDOR SERVICES AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"VENDOR SERVICES AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Vendors and Facilities","primaryUse":"Goods, services, technology, production, logistics, and vendors.","filename":"06_Vendor_Services_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/06_Vendor_Services_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Vendor Services Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Vendor for the goods, professional services, technology, staffing, logistics, production, equipment, transportation, food, merchandise, or other deliverables described in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Orders, Deliverables, and Acceptance","body":"Vendor shall deliver the goods and services, milestones, specifications, quantities, staffing, locations, service levels, and documentation in Schedule 1. RTBO may inspect and test deliverables. Acceptance occurs only after written acceptance or use beyond the stated review period, and does not waive latent defects, warranties, fraud, or indemnity rights."},{"title":"Pricing, Invoices, and No Unauthorized Charges","body":"Prices are firm unless Schedule 1 provides an adjustment method. Invoices must identify the agreement, purchase order if any, dates, units, approved expenses, taxes, and supporting records. RTBO may dispute charges in good faith and pay undisputed amounts. No fee, renewal, minimum, surcharge, expense, or subcontractor charge is authorized unless stated or preapproved in writing."},{"title":"Vendor Personnel and Subcontractors","body":"Vendor is responsible for personnel qualifications, supervision, pay, taxes, safety, conduct, screening, licenses, and legal eligibility. Subcontracting requires prior written approval and does not release Vendor. Vendor shall flow down confidentiality, security, insurance, safeguarding, ownership, audit, and compliance obligations."},{"title":"Warranties","body":"Vendor warrants that deliverables are professional, timely, conforming, safe, merchantable where applicable, fit for the disclosed purpose, free of liens and malicious code, noninfringing, and compliant with specifications and law. Vendor shall promptly repair, replace, reperformance, or refund defective deliverables, without limiting other remedies."},{"title":"Technology, Accessibility, and Security","body":"Technology deliverables shall meet the service levels, backup, recovery, incident response, data location, deletion, interoperability, support, and accessibility requirements in Schedule 1. Vendor shall not use RTBO or customer data to train models, advertise, profile, sell, or develop unrelated products without express written consent."},{"title":"Business Continuity and Transition","body":"Vendor shall maintain reasonable continuity and disaster-recovery plans. At expiration or termination, Vendor shall provide orderly transition assistance, return RTBO property and data in a usable format, certify deletion of remaining copies except lawful archives, and avoid service interruption."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Attach a detailed statement of work. Vendors handling payments, student data, personal information, transportation, food, technology, or minors may require specialized security, licensing, insurance, and regulatory addenda.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Vendor","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Statement of Work / Purchase Order","[NUMBER / DATE]"],["Goods / Services / Specifications","[DETAILS]"],["Milestones / Delivery Locations","[DETAILS]"],["Price / Taxes / Expenses","[DETAILS]"],["Invoice / Payment Terms","[DETAILS]"],["Acceptance Testing / Review Period","[DETAILS]"],["Warranties / Remedies","[DETAILS]"],["Service Levels / Support","[DETAILS]"],["Vendor Personnel / Subcontractors","[DETAILS]"],["Licenses / Screening / Safeguarding","[DETAILS]"],["Technology / Accessibility / Security","[DETAILS]"],["Data / Subprocessors / Retention","[DETAILS]"],["Ownership / License","[DETAILS]"],["Business Continuity / Transition","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance","[DETAILS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Term / Termination","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","VENDOR"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":43,"fileSize":419731,"sha256":"d464efd44e270ea79097c3d900002f86149aeb9d53783c91c82de7c2cf67aed9"},{"key":"library-07-independent-contractor-agreement","code":"07","title":"INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Workforce and Contractors","primaryUse":"Non-official contractors when classification facts support it.","filename":"07_Independent_Contractor_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/07_Independent_Contractor_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Independent Contractor Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Contractor for discrete professional or operational services described in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Services and Results","body":"Contractor shall produce the defined results and deliverables in Schedule 1 using Contractor’s independent skill and judgment. RTBO may define desired outcomes, deadlines, legal and safety requirements, interfaces, acceptance criteria, and customer commitments, but will not control Contractor’s lawful day-to-day manner and means except as necessary to protect people, property, confidential information, and compliance."},{"title":"Independent Enterprise and Nonexclusivity","body":"Contractor represents that Contractor is customarily engaged in an independently established business, may market and provide services to others, may accept or reject proposed projects, and is not economically dependent on a guaranteed flow of RTBO work. No minimum work, exclusivity, tenure, seniority, or continued engagement is promised."},{"title":"Personnel, Tools, Place, and Schedule","body":"Except as Schedule 1 states, Contractor selects and pays qualified personnel, supplies ordinary tools and equipment, chooses work location and sequence, and controls schedule while meeting milestones and coordination needs. Any approved substitute remains subject to credentials, confidentiality, security, and safety requirements, and Contractor remains responsible for performance."},{"title":"Compensation, Expenses, and Business Risk","body":"Contractor is paid by project, deliverable, assignment, unit, or other method in Schedule 1 and bears ordinary business expenses and risk of efficient performance. Approved reimbursable expenses require documentation. Contractor may realize profit or loss through managerial skill, investment, staffing, and cost control, subject to law."},{"title":"Taxes, Benefits, and Legal Reclassification","body":"Contractor is responsible for required tax filings, estimated taxes, permits, licenses, insurance, and benefits for Contractor and personnel. Contractor is not eligible for employee benefits unless required by law. If an agency or court determines reclassification is required, the parties shall cooperate in lawful correction; no waiver releases nonwaivable rights or obligations."},{"title":"No Authority; No Holding Out","body":"Contractor is not an agent and may not bind RTBO, sign contracts, incur debt, make warranties, hire on RTBO’s behalf, or represent authority unless a separate written authorization expressly grants it."},{"title":"Work Product","body":"Upon full payment, specifically commissioned work product identified as deliverable in Schedule 1 is assigned to RTBO to the extent legally assignable, excluding Contractor’s pre-existing tools and general know-how. Contractor grants RTBO a perpetual license to embedded pre-existing materials necessary to use the deliverables and shall secure equivalent rights from approved personnel."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Classification depends on the actual relationship under applicable law, not the title of this agreement. Before use, RTBO must evaluate control, opportunity for profit or loss, investment, permanence, skill, integration, outside business activity, tax treatment, and all other relevant factors. Use an employment agreement when required.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Contractor","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Services / Deliverables","[DETAILED DESCRIPTION]"],["Locations / Events","[VENUES, GAMES, DATES, TIMES]"],["Fees and Payment","[RATES, INVOICING, DUE DATE, LATE CHARGES IF LAWFUL]"],["Expenses / Travel","[AUTHORIZED EXPENSES, MILEAGE, LODGING, PER DIEM]"],["Cancellation / Rescheduling","[NOTICE WINDOWS AND FEES]"],["Insurance Requirements","[TYPES, LIMITS, CERTIFICATES, ADDITIONAL INSUREDS]"],["Contract Administrators","RTBO: [NAME/EMAIL/PHONE] | Counterparty: [NAME/EMAIL/PHONE]"],["Notices","RTBO: [ADDRESS/EMAIL] | Counterparty: [ADDRESS/EMAIL]"],["Convenience Termination Notice","[NUMBER] days"],["Liability Cap, if any","[NONE unless a specific dollar amount is entered]"],["Special Terms","[ADDITIONAL NEGOTIATED TERMS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","CONTRACTOR"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":420015,"sha256":"caa7f9fe23939a6e784a30d0133d32280537bf80bed5f8b5ac9db3568d4e667f"},{"key":"library-08-customer-agreement","code":"08","title":"CUSTOMER AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"CUSTOMER AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Sponsors and Customers","primaryUse":"Business or consumer purchases, registrations, subscriptions, or services.","filename":"08_Customer_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/08_Customer_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Customer Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Customer for the purchase or use of the products, subscriptions, registrations, consulting, officiating, assigning, training, media, technology, or other services in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Order and Services","body":"Customer purchases only the items, services, quantities, term, users, events, and deliverables stated in Schedule 1 or an accepted order. Customer shall provide accurate information, timely cooperation, authorized access, and a safe and lawful environment. RTBO may rely on instructions from Customer’s designated administrator."},{"title":"Accounts and Authorized Users","body":"Customer is responsible for authorized-user access, credentials, permissions, and activity, except to the extent caused by RTBO’s security failure. Customer shall promptly report suspected compromise. Users must comply with applicable terms, codes of conduct, acceptable-use rules, and age or consent requirements."},{"title":"Charges, Billing, Taxes, and Renewal","body":"Customer shall pay stated charges and applicable taxes by the due date. Recurring services renew only as disclosed in Schedule 1 and applicable checkout terms. RTBO shall provide required renewal notices and cancellation methods. Failed payments may result in suspension after legally required notice. Chargebacks do not replace the dispute process."},{"title":"Cancellation, Refunds, Credits, and Changes","body":"The cancellation and refund policy appears in Schedule 1 and does not limit nonwaivable rights. Event, roster, seat, subscription, or service changes may affect pricing and availability. RTBO may cancel or modify for safety, legality, insufficient enrollment, venue, staffing, or force majeure and will provide the stated remedy."},{"title":"Acceptable Use and Conduct","body":"Customer shall not misuse systems, scrape or resell content, infringe rights, upload unlawful or harmful material, bypass security, impersonate others, harass participants, interfere with officiating, or use services for gambling manipulation, discrimination, fraud, or unsafe conduct. RTBO may suspend access to address a credible risk."},{"title":"Service Disclaimer","body":"RTBO will perform services professionally but does not guarantee a specific assignment, officiating result, game outcome, rating, placement, credential, scholarship, employment, admission, athletic performance, revenue, or third-party decision unless Schedule 1 expressly provides an objective guarantee and remedy."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Consumer, automatic-renewal, refund, privacy, accessibility, tax, and online-contract rules vary by jurisdiction. Do not use business-to-business limitations against consumers where prohibited, and clearly present recurring charges before enrollment.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Customer","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Order / Registration / Subscription","[DETAILS]"],["Customer Type / Authorized Users","[BUSINESS / CONSUMER; USERS]"],["Services / Deliverables / Access","[DETAILS]"],["Term / Start Date","[DETAILS]"],["Price / Taxes / Billing Method","[DETAILS]"],["Recurring Charge / Renewal","[NONE OR FULL DISCLOSURE]"],["Renewal Notice / Cancellation Method","[DETAILS]"],["Refund / Credit / Transfer Policy","[DETAILS]"],["Event Change / Force Majeure Remedy","[DETAILS]"],["Customer Responsibilities","[DETAILS]"],["Account / Acceptable-Use Rules","[DETAILS]"],["Data / Privacy / Media","[DETAILS]"],["Support / Service Level","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance, if applicable","[DETAILS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","CUSTOMER"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":43,"fileSize":419720,"sha256":"7815acecdd3c791a78094c2aa8ce8d712cbd65cf0d7d27b98ccb6fc2b221f0bc"},{"key":"library-09-master-officiating-and-assigning-services-agreement","code":"09","title":"MASTER OFFICIATING AND ASSIGNING SERVICES AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"MASTER OFFICIATING AND ASSIGNING SERVICES AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Assigning Services","primaryUse":"Recurring or multi-season client relationships with statements of work.","filename":"09_Master_Officiating_and_Assigning_Services_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/09_Master_Officiating_and_Assigning_Services_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Master Officiating and Assigning Services Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Client and establishes the complete legal framework for recurring sports-officiating and assignment-management services. Each season, league, event, or workstream may be documented in a signed Statement of Work.","clauses":[{"title":"Statements of Work and Order of Precedence","body":"No service is required until authorized in a signed Statement of Work or documented order. A Statement of Work may add detail but changes this Agreement only when it identifies the provision changed and is signed by authorized representatives. Conflicts are resolved in this order: signed amendment, Statement of Work special terms, this Agreement, then referenced operational documents."},{"title":"Assignment Administration","body":"RTBO may recruit, credential, classify, schedule, notify, replace, evaluate, and communicate with officials and may use a technology platform. RTBO shall apply disclosed eligibility, availability, conflict, travel, workload, and competency standards in good faith. Client shall provide complete schedules, contacts, venue data, game requirements, and changes by agreed deadlines."},{"title":"Coverage Standard and Limits","body":"RTBO shall use commercially reasonable efforts to fill covered contests with qualified personnel. Unless a Statement of Work states an express service level and remedy, RTBO does not guarantee uninterrupted coverage where shortages, late changes, emergencies, refusals, weather, transportation, illness, safety conditions, or force majeure interfere. RTBO shall promptly communicate known material coverage risks."},{"title":"Official Status and Payment Model","body":"Each Statement of Work shall identify who contracts with, controls, pays, insures, and reports compensation for officials and whether RTBO acts as principal, disclosed payment administrator, platform provider, or assignor. The parties shall not structure or administer the relationship to evade employment, tax, wage, benefit, or reporting law."},{"title":"Client Event Responsibilities","body":"Client controls the event, venue, teams, schedule, admission, coaches, participants, spectators, table crew, security, medical response, and premises. Client shall prevent harassment and retaliation against officials, provide safe access and departure, and investigate site or participant misconduct. RTBO may withdraw personnel from unsafe or materially noncompliant conditions."},{"title":"Fees, Deposits, Reserves, and Reconciliation","body":"The Statement of Work shall separate assignment fees, official fees, platform or administration fees, expenses, taxes, deposits, reserves, late changes, cancellation charges, and payment processing. When RTBO distributes funds to officials, Client shall fund on the stated schedule and RTBO may suspend new assignments for delinquency after notice."},{"title":"Performance Management and Complaints","body":"Client may submit timely, fact-based feedback through the designated process. RTBO controls personnel and assignment decisions consistent with its role and law. Complaints involving discrimination, harassment, abuse, retaliation, fraud, safety, or integrity shall be escalated promptly. Neither party shall publish knowingly false or retaliatory statements."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Use this agreement for recurring or multi-program relationships. Each Statement of Work must identify the sport, governing rules, coverage obligations, payment structure, operational responsibilities, and order of precedence.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Client","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Statement of Work / Season","[NAME AND DATES]"],["Sports / Divisions / Levels","[DETAILS]"],["Covered Contests","[ESTIMATED NUMBER, SCHEDULE SOURCE]"],["Crew Model","[POSITIONS, CREW SIZE, ALTERNATES]"],["Assignment Services","[RECRUIT, CREDENTIAL, ASSIGN, REPLACE, EVALUATE]"],["Coverage Service Level / Remedy","[IF NEGOTIATED]"],["Official Contracting / Payor Model","[CLIENT / RTBO / DIRECT / ADMINISTRATOR]"],["Fees and Funding","[ALL COMPONENTS AND DUE DATES]"],["Schedule Change / Cancellation","[TERMS]"],["Venue / Security / Medical","[CLIENT DUTIES]"],["Reports and Data","[DELIVERABLES, ACCESS, RETENTION]"],["Insurance","[REQUIREMENTS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[CONTACTS]"],["Term / Termination","[TERMS]"],["Special Terms","[TERMS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","CLIENT"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":420135,"sha256":"aae74f4ab28059068703ca3726e6dd3e5b29a73320c3d0189a1a50183d7a9a75"},{"key":"library-10-league-and-conference-assigning-agreement","code":"10","title":"LEAGUE AND CONFERENCE ASSIGNING AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"LEAGUE AND CONFERENCE ASSIGNING AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Assigning Services","primaryUse":"Centralized assigning for leagues, conferences, districts, or associations.","filename":"10_League_and_Conference_Assigning_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/10_League_and_Conference_Assigning_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This League and Conference Assigning Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified league, conference, association, district, or governing organization for centralized assignment and related officiating administration.","clauses":[{"title":"Appointment and Authority","body":"League appoints RTBO as [exclusive/nonexclusive] assignor for the competitions in Schedule 1. RTBO’s authority is limited to recruiting, credential review, assignment, replacement, evaluation, communications, payment administration, and other listed functions. League retains governance, eligibility, competition policy, sanctions, championships, and member oversight unless expressly delegated."},{"title":"Assignment Criteria and Integrity","body":"RTBO shall use good-faith criteria including qualifications, rules proficiency, performance, availability, travel, workload, crew balance, development, conflicts, and governing-body requirements. League shall not require assignments based on unlawful discrimination, favoritism, retaliation, gambling interest, or improper influence. Material conflicts and integrity concerns must be disclosed."},{"title":"Member Organization Obligations","body":"League shall bind or obtain written acknowledgment from covered members regarding schedules, deadlines, fees, security, facility standards, conduct, change notices, complaint procedures, and payment. League remains responsible for obligations it assumes and for communicating enforceable requirements to members."},{"title":"Rules, Mechanics, Training, and Evaluations","body":"League shall identify the applicable rules, bulletins, mechanics, points of emphasis, replay or challenge protocols, and required training. RTBO may conduct clinics, testing, observations, ratings, mentoring, and development as stated in Schedule 1. Evaluation data access and appeals shall follow published policy and applicable privacy law."},{"title":"Postseason and High-Impact Assignments","body":"Selection authority, criteria, approval rights, recusals, alternates, confidentiality, and announcement timing for postseason, championship, televised, rivalry, or high-risk contests must be documented in Schedule 1. No person is guaranteed selection."},{"title":"Discipline, Complaints, and Appeals","body":"The parties shall allocate investigation and decision authority for officiating performance, conduct, eligibility, safeguarding, and member complaints. Immediate interim action may be taken for safety or integrity. Any promised notice, response, review, or appeal process must be stated in policy and applied consistently, subject to law."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Attach and approve the competition calendar, bylaws, assignment authority, conflict rules, fee schedule, disciplinary roles, appeals process, and member-school obligations. Public member institutions may require separate approvals or joinders.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["League / Conference","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["League / Conference / Season","[DETAILS]"],["Appointment","[EXCLUSIVE / NONEXCLUSIVE; TERM]"],["Sports / Divisions / Governing Rules","[DETAILS]"],["Member Organizations / Joinders","[LIST / PROCESS]"],["Covered Contests / Schedule Source","[DETAILS]"],["Crew Model / Credentials","[DETAILS]"],["Assignment Criteria / Conflict Rules","[DETAILS]"],["Training / Testing / Mechanics","[DETAILS]"],["Evaluation / Ratings / Data Access","[DETAILS]"],["Postseason Selection / Approval","[DETAILS]"],["Discipline / Complaints / Appeals","[DETAILS]"],["Official Contracting / Payment Model","[DETAILS]"],["Fees / Member Funding / Reconciliation","[DETAILS]"],["Schedule Changes / Cancellations","[DETAILS]"],["Security / Medical / Member Duties","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance","[DETAILS]"],["Administrators / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","LEAGUE / CONFERENCE"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":43,"fileSize":419793,"sha256":"249e342680c4eb70018a89cf3f9cbfbb8945bfd52efda73a166961c8798773fa"},{"key":"library-11-tournament-showcase-and-special-event-officiating-agreement","code":"11","title":"TOURNAMENT, SHOWCASE, AND SPECIAL EVENT OFFICIATING AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"TOURNAMENT, SHOWCASE, AND SPECIAL EVENT OFFICIATING AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Events and Tournaments","primaryUse":"Compressed, multi-court, or special-event officiating.","filename":"11_Tournament_Showcase_and_Special_Event_Officiating_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/11_Tournament_Showcase_and_Special_Event_Officiating_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Tournament, Showcase, and Special Event Officiating Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Event Operator for officiating and assignment services for the event described in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Event Services and Staffing Plan","body":"RTBO shall recruit and assign the crew count, positions, supervisors, evaluators, alternates, and administrative staff in Schedule 1. Event Operator shall provide a complete schedule, divisions, playing rules, court map, venue access, check-in plan, contacts, and change authority by the stated deadline."},{"title":"Workload, Rest, and Assignment Safeguards","body":"The parties shall follow stated limits on consecutive games, daily games, rest, travel, and high-risk assignments. RTBO may adjust crews to address fatigue, heat, illness, injury, performance, safety, conflicts, or schedule disruption. No official is required to continue when conditions present an unreasonable safety risk."},{"title":"Event Operations","body":"Event Operator is responsible for facility readiness, court equipment, scorekeepers and timers, security, emergency medical response, participant eligibility, crowd and team conduct, parking, credentials, hospitality, and a continuously available command contact. RTBO may pause or withdraw services from an unsafe court or venue after reasonable notice when circumstances permit."},{"title":"Schedule Lock and Change Control","body":"The schedule-lock date and authorized change method appear in Schedule 1. Added games, shortened turnarounds, venue changes, or material time shifts after lock are subject to availability and adjustment fees. Only designated contacts may authorize changes that affect costs or staffing."},{"title":"Funding and Payment","body":"Event Operator shall fund deposits, official game fees, assignment and administration fees, travel, lodging, per diem, and reserves on the schedule stated. RTBO may withhold publication or suspend coverage if required funding is not received. Final reconciliation shall account for completed, cancelled, added, and compensable minimum assignments."},{"title":"Cancellation, Weather, and Abandonment","body":"Schedule 1 shall specify refund and fee treatment for full cancellation, partial cancellation, delayed start, shortened games, venue closure, weather, team withdrawal, and abandonment. Officials who report or begin travel may be entitled to minimum or travel compensation even if play does not occur."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Multi-court and compressed events require precise schedules, rest rules, staffing assumptions, emergency contacts, lodging, transportation, payment funding, and cancellation terms. Attach the final event grid and operating plan.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Event Operator","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Event / Operator / Sanctioning Body","[DETAILS]"],["Dates / Venues / Courts","[DETAILS]"],["Sports / Divisions / Rules","[DETAILS]"],["Game Grid / Schedule-Lock Date","[ATTACHMENT / DEADLINE]"],["Crew Positions / Officials / Alternates","[DETAILS]"],["Supervisors / Evaluators / Administrators","[DETAILS]"],["Workload / Consecutive-Game / Rest Limits","[DETAILS]"],["Report / Check-In / Change Process","[DETAILS]"],["Official Fees / Assignment Fees","[DETAILS]"],["Deposit / Funding / Reserve / Reconciliation","[DETAILS]"],["Travel / Lodging / Per Diem","[DETAILS]"],["Cancellation / Weather / Minimum Fees","[DETAILS]"],["Security / Medical / Site Operations","[DETAILS]"],["Participant / Minor Safeguarding","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance / Permits","[DETAILS]"],["Command Contacts / Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","EVENT OPERATOR"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":420056,"sha256":"0bd58d074e6589591bede6e1a6a204b456fb34c8d3d536113c788f234d6a9de0"},{"key":"library-12-official-assignment-acceptance-and-game-confirmation","code":"12","title":"OFFICIAL ASSIGNMENT ACCEPTANCE AND GAME CONFIRMATION","documentTitle":"OFFICIAL ASSIGNMENT ACCEPTANCE AND GAME CONFIRMATION","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Officials and Assignments","primaryUse":"A specific game or event confirmation.","filename":"12_Official_Assignment_Acceptance_and_Game_Confirmation.docx","url":"library/docx/12_Official_Assignment_Acceptance_and_Game_Confirmation.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Official Assignment Acceptance and Game Confirmation records a specific assignment offered by Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and accepted by Official. It supplements, but does not require, any broader officials agreement and is independently enforceable for the confirmed assignment.","clauses":[{"title":"Confirmed Assignment","body":"Official accepts the exact assignment described in Schedule 1 and confirms availability, credentials, absence of undisclosed conflicts, and ability to arrive by the report time. Acceptance is personal and may not be transferred without RTBO approval."},{"title":"Performance Duties","body":"Official shall review event instructions, wear required uniform, carry required equipment, officiate under the identified rules and mechanics, exercise independent judgment, cooperate with the crew and site administration, and submit required game, incident, ejection, or expense reports by the deadline."},{"title":"Change and Withdrawal","body":"Official shall promptly report any circumstance affecting availability or eligibility. RTBO may change position, crew, court, or similar operational details when reasonably necessary, but a material change to date, location, compensation, or workload requires Official’s acceptance unless an emergency policy expressly applies."},{"title":"Fee and Payment","body":"The stated fee is full compensation for the assignment except approved travel and expenses. Payment timing and payor are stated in Schedule 1. Official shall provide complete tax and payment information. A client payment delay is allocated as stated and may not be implied."},{"title":"Cancellation and Report-Time Minimum","body":"Cancellation, postponement, weather, travel, and minimum fees are governed solely by Schedule 1. Official must mitigate avoidable expenses and follow instructions before beginning travel when conditions are uncertain."},{"title":"Safety and Integrity","body":"Official may leave or refuse an assignment when there is a reasonable, good-faith belief of imminent danger, unlawful discrimination, abuse, or integrity compromise, after notifying RTBO or emergency authorities when feasible. Gambling, bribery, score manipulation, unauthorized disclosure, and retaliation are prohibited."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Complete one confirmation for each game, event block, or assignment set. This document should match the assignment platform and identifies the exact fee, location, rules, position, travel, cancellation, and reporting terms.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Official","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Assignment ID","[ID]"],["Sport / Level / Gender / Rules","[DETAILS]"],["Date / Game Time / Report Time","[DETAILS]"],["Venue / Address / Court","[DETAILS]"],["Teams / Event","[DETAILS]"],["Position / Crew","[REFEREE / U1 / U2 / ALTERNATE / OTHER]"],["Fee / Payor","[AMOUNT; PARTY RESPONSIBLE]"],["Payment Timing / Method","[DETAILS]"],["Travel / Lodging / Expenses","[DETAILS]"],["Uniform / Equipment","[DETAILS]"],["Site / Assignor Contacts","[DETAILS]"],["Cancellation / Postponement","[DETAILS]"],["Reports Due","[DETAILS]"],["Special Instructions","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","OFFICIAL"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":419864,"sha256":"d3810f4dae4b16c28a82e748a5f01ebcdbd34d96d82c5bde15e48753db6ee25f"},{"key":"library-13-venue-and-facility-use-agreement","code":"13","title":"VENUE AND FACILITY USE AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"VENUE AND FACILITY USE AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Vendors and Facilities","primaryUse":"Gyms, classrooms, courts, meeting, and event spaces.","filename":"13_Venue_and_Facility_Use_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/13_Venue_and_Facility_Use_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Venue and Facility Use Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Facility Owner or Operator for temporary use of the facility identified in Schedule 1 for games, training, events, meetings, media, or related activities.","clauses":[{"title":"License to Use Facility","body":"Facility grants RTBO a limited, nonexclusive, revocable license to use only the spaces, dates, hours, entrances, parking, storage, utilities, equipment, and ancillary areas stated in Schedule 1. No leasehold or property interest is created. Access for setup and teardown must be included."},{"title":"Facility Condition and Legal Compliance","body":"Facility represents that it has authority to grant use and will maintain premises, systems, courts, seating, exits, lighting, restrooms, accessibility features, fire protection, and provided equipment in safe and legally compliant condition. Facility shall disclose known hazards, restrictions, construction, shared use, and emergency procedures."},{"title":"Operational Responsibilities","body":"Schedule 1 allocates security, crowd control, medical coverage, custodial service, trash, concessions, scoreboards, tables, chairs, audiovisual equipment, locker or dressing areas, keys, parking, signage, internet, utilities, and event staffing. Each party is responsible for the areas and personnel under its control."},{"title":"Capacity, Conduct, and Restricted Activities","body":"RTBO shall observe lawful capacity, access, food, alcohol, tobacco, weapons, animals, decoration, noise, floor-protection, and vendor restrictions disclosed before execution. Facility may remove a person presenting a safety or legal risk, but shall not interfere with officiating or discriminate unlawfully."},{"title":"Property; Damage; Inspection","body":"The parties shall conduct pre- and post-use inspections when practical. RTBO is responsible for physical damage to Facility property to the extent caused by RTBO or persons under its control, ordinary wear excepted. Facility shall document damage and reasonable repair costs. Lost property procedures are stated in Schedule 1."},{"title":"Cancellation and Unavailability","body":"Facility shall promptly notify RTBO of closures or conditions affecting use. Schedule 1 shall state deposits, cancellation windows, refunds, substitute space, weather, utility failure, and remedies. Facility remains responsible for refunds or agreed alternatives when it cannot provide substantially conforming space, except as stated for force majeure."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. A venue agreement should be supported by inspection, occupancy and permit review, emergency planning, insurance certificates, accessibility review, and clear allocation of security, medical, cleaning, equipment, and property responsibilities.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Facility Owner / Operator","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Facility / Address","[DETAILS]"],["Licensed Spaces / Capacity","[DETAILS]"],["Use / Event","[DETAILS]"],["Access / Setup / Event / Teardown Times","[DETAILS]"],["Rental Fee / Deposit / Payment","[DETAILS]"],["Cancellation / Closure / Substitute Space","[DETAILS]"],["Provided Equipment / Utilities / Internet","[DETAILS]"],["Security / Crowd Control","[RESPONSIBLE PARTY / LEVEL]"],["Medical / Emergency / Fire Plan","[DETAILS]"],["Custodial / Trash / Damage Inspection","[DETAILS]"],["Parking / Entrances / Credentials","[DETAILS]"],["Accessibility / Accommodations","[DETAILS]"],["Food / Concessions / Vendors","[DETAILS]"],["Restricted Activities / Floor Protection","[DETAILS]"],["Permits / Licenses / Taxes","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance / Additional Insured","[DETAILS]"],["Facility / RTBO Contacts and Notices","[DETAILS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","FACILITY OWNER / OPERATOR"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":43,"fileSize":419793,"sha256":"1d2e845901696f7df95035a390cb255713cd461f7bea9edc3eff268d8030b0d2"},{"key":"library-14-data-privacy-confidentiality-and-security-agreement","code":"14","title":"DATA PRIVACY, CONFIDENTIALITY, AND SECURITY AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"DATA PRIVACY, CONFIDENTIALITY, AND SECURITY AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Privacy and Confidentiality","primaryUse":"Protected personal, student, assignment, evaluation, and system data.","filename":"14_Data_Privacy_Confidentiality_and_Security_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/14_Data_Privacy_Confidentiality_and_Security_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Data Privacy, Confidentiality, and Security Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified party and governs personal information, education records, credentials, payment data, assignment data, evaluations, media, system data, and other protected information exchanged or processed in connection with sports, education, and business services.","clauses":[{"title":"Data Roles; Instructions; Purpose Limitation","body":"Schedule 1 identifies each data category, data subject, source, system, party role, authorized purpose, and lawful basis or permission. Recipient shall process data only on documented instructions and only to perform the authorized services, unless law requires otherwise. Recipient shall notify the owner if an instruction appears unlawful."},{"title":"Minimum Necessary Access and Accuracy","body":"The parties shall minimize collection, fields, users, exports, and retention. Recipient shall implement role-based access, unique accounts, strong authentication, least privilege, logging, periodic access review, and procedures to correct or annotate inaccurate information when required."},{"title":"Security Program","body":"Recipient shall maintain a written, risk-based security program appropriate to data sensitivity and volume, including workforce training, confidentiality commitments, secure configuration, encryption in transit and at rest where reasonable, vulnerability and patch management, malware protection, backup, recovery testing, vendor risk management, secure development, physical safeguards, and verified destruction."},{"title":"Education Records","body":"When Recipient handles education records under a school-official exception, Recipient is under the educational agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, performs the defined institutional service, accesses only records for legitimate educational interests, and shall not redisclose or use them for another purpose except as legally permitted. The agency controls annual-notice and record-disclosure obligations."},{"title":"Security Incident and Breach Response","body":"Recipient shall immediately investigate suspected unauthorized access, acquisition, use, alteration, loss, destruction, or disclosure; contain and mitigate harm; preserve logs and evidence; and notify the owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four hours. Notices shall include known facts, affected data and systems, dates, containment, risks, law-enforcement constraints, and remediation. The parties shall coordinate legally required notices without delaying mandatory deadlines."},{"title":"Subprocessors and Data Location","body":"Recipient shall not permit a subprocessor to access protected data without written authorization and a contract imposing equivalent duties. Schedule 1 lists approved subprocessors and storage or access locations. Recipient remains responsible for subprocessor performance and shall provide notice of material changes."},{"title":"Requests, Legal Process, Audit, and Cooperation","body":"Recipient shall promptly forward data-subject, parent, student, regulator, school, discovery, or legal-process requests and shall not respond except as authorized or legally required. Recipient shall provide reasonable compliance information, independent assessments, remediation evidence, and audit cooperation, subject to security and confidentiality safeguards."},{"title":"Return, Deletion, and Retention","body":"At termination or request, Recipient shall return data in an agreed usable format and securely delete remaining copies, including backups as they cycle, unless law requires retention. Any retained data remains protected and may be used only for the retention purpose. Recipient shall certify deletion on request."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Complete the data inventory, role allocation, approved purposes, systems, retention, subprocessors, cross-border locations, incident contacts, and education-record terms before any protected data is shared. This agreement is not a substitute for any legally required HIPAA, payment-card, state privacy, or international data-processing addendum.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Data Recipient / Service Provider","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Data Owner / Controller","[PARTY]"],["Recipient / Processor","[PARTY]"],["Services / Purpose","[DETAILS]"],["Data Subjects","[OFFICIALS, STUDENTS, PARENTS, STAFF, CUSTOMERS, ETC.]"],["Data Categories","[IDENTIFIERS, CONTACT, EDUCATION, PAYMENT, EVALUATION, MEDIA, ETC.]"],["Sensitive Data","[DETAILS OR NONE]"],["Systems / Transfer Methods","[DETAILS]"],["Authorized Users / Access","[DETAILS]"],["Education Records / Direct Control","[DETAILS OR NOT APPLICABLE]"],["Retention / Deletion","[PER CATEGORY]"],["Approved Subprocessors","[LIST]"],["Data Locations","[LIST]"],["Security Requirements","[SPECIFIC CONTROLS / STANDARDS]"],["Incident Contacts","[24/7 CONTACTS]"],["Notification Cooperation / Costs","[ALLOCATION]"],["Audit Evidence","[SOC 2, PEN TEST, QUESTIONNAIRE, ETC.]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","DATA RECIPIENT / SERVICE PROVIDER"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":47,"fileSize":420290,"sha256":"b8c976f643ab8d83b89fb87aadcf69c7915ed3f196f4162e56ed30e74cd27b6e"},{"key":"library-15-mutual-nondisclosure-agreement","code":"15","title":"MUTUAL NONDISCLOSURE AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"MUTUAL NONDISCLOSURE AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Privacy and Confidentiality","primaryUse":"Precontract or project confidentiality.","filename":"15_Mutual_Nondisclosure_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/15_Mutual_Nondisclosure_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Mutual Nondisclosure Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified party to permit evaluation or performance of a potential or existing business relationship while protecting confidential information.","clauses":[{"title":"Confidential Information","body":"Confidential Information means nonpublic information disclosed in any form that is marked confidential or that a reasonable person would understand is confidential, including business plans, pricing, contracts, financials, technology, security, credentials, assignments, evaluations, personnel, customers, students, participants, investigations, methods, and trade secrets. Oral disclosure should be identified as confidential when made and, when practical, summarized in writing."},{"title":"Exclusions","body":"Confidential Information excludes information the recipient can document was lawfully known without duty, becomes public without breach, is received lawfully from a third party without duty, or is independently developed without use of the disclosure. A combination is not excluded merely because individual elements are public."},{"title":"Use and Protection","body":"Recipient shall use Confidential Information only for the Purpose in Schedule 1, disclose it only to representatives with a need to know and equivalent duties, and protect it with at least reasonable care and no less than the care used for similar information. Recipient is responsible for representatives’ breaches."},{"title":"Required Disclosure","body":"If legally compelled, Recipient shall, when lawful, give prompt notice and reasonable assistance so Discloser may seek protection. Recipient shall disclose only what counsel advises is required and use reasonable efforts to obtain confidential treatment. Public-records requests are governed by applicable law and the public entity’s legal determination."},{"title":"No License; No Obligation","body":"Disclosure grants no ownership, license, agency, exclusivity, or commitment to transact. Information is provided as-is for evaluation, except that neither party may knowingly misrepresent material facts. Each party bears its own evaluation costs."},{"title":"Return, Destruction, Term, and Remedies","body":"Upon request or end of the Purpose, Recipient shall return or destroy Confidential Information except archival copies required by law or routine backup, which remain protected. Duties continue for the period in Schedule 1 and for trade secrets as long as protected by law. Unauthorized use may cause irreparable harm for which equitable relief may be available, in addition to lawful remedies."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. An NDA does not replace a data-processing agreement, intellectual-property license, employment agreement, noncompetition agreement, public-records analysis, or privilege protocol. Public entities should review disclosure obligations before execution.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Receiving / Disclosing Party","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Purpose","[EVALUATION / PROJECT / RELATIONSHIP]"],["Permitted Representatives","[CATEGORIES]"],["Disclosure Period","[DATES]"],["Confidentiality Period","[NUMBER] years; trade secrets while legally protected"],["Excluded / Preapproved Disclosures","[DETAILS]"],["Special Security Requirements","[DETAILS]"],["Notices","[CONTACTS]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","RECEIVING / DISCLOSING PARTY"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":39,"fileSize":418967,"sha256":"0d0e5a8eb25a46a1fa7510be0978d8f0b3a1df2414ec07507768cca6e11843c5"},{"key":"library-16-evaluator-observer-and-training-personnel-agreement","code":"16","title":"EVALUATOR, OBSERVER, AND TRAINING PERSONNEL AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"EVALUATOR, OBSERVER, AND TRAINING PERSONNEL AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Training and Education","primaryUse":"Evaluators, clinicians, trainers, mentors, and observers.","filename":"16_Evaluator_Observer_and_Training_Personnel_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/16_Evaluator_Observer_and_Training_Personnel_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Evaluator, Observer, and Training Personnel Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the individual providing evaluation, observation, instruction, mentoring, rules, video, curriculum, or clinician services.","clauses":[{"title":"Services and Professional Standard","body":"Evaluator shall perform the observations, reports, instruction, feedback, scoring, video review, curriculum, mentoring, or administrative services in Schedule 1 competently, impartially, timely, and according to approved criteria. Evaluator shall distinguish observed facts, rule analysis, professional opinion, and recommended development action."},{"title":"Independence, Conflicts, and Integrity","body":"Evaluator shall disclose personal, financial, employment, family, team, betting, assignment, competitive, or other conflicts and recuse when impartiality may reasonably be questioned. Evaluator shall not solicit favors, condition ratings on personal benefit, retaliate, manipulate rankings, disclose selection information, or promise assignments or advancement."},{"title":"Evaluation Records and Access","body":"Reports, ratings, notes, recordings, and rankings are confidential and may be accessed or disclosed only as authorized. Evaluator shall use approved systems, avoid unprotected devices or messaging for sensitive information, and return or delete records after submission. Any promised subject access, comments, appeal, correction, or visibility restriction shall follow written policy."},{"title":"Instructional Conduct and Safeguarding","body":"Evaluator shall maintain professional boundaries, avoid harassment and discrimination, follow one-on-one interaction and travel rules, and report suspected abuse directly as required by law. Instruction must not require unsafe physical activity or humiliation. Medical or emergency concerns shall be referred to qualified personnel."},{"title":"Materials and Recordings","body":"Schedule 1 identifies pre-existing materials and commissioned work product. Evaluator may use RTBO materials only for assigned services and may not copy, publish, train unrelated systems, or commercialize confidential curriculum, footage, evaluations, or participant data without written approval."},{"title":"Compensation and Expenses","body":"Evaluator shall be paid the stated fee after timely completion and acceptance of required reports or sessions. Approved travel and expenses require documentation. Cancellation, postponement, minimum, and late-report consequences are stated in Schedule 1 and applied lawfully."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Use the separate employment agreement when the facts support employee status. Evaluation criteria, confidentiality, data access, conflicts, appeal roles, compensation, and ownership of training materials must be completed before service.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Evaluator / Trainer","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Role / Services","[EVALUATOR, OBSERVER, TRAINER, CLINICIAN, ETC.]"],["Events / Courses / Dates","[DETAILS]"],["Criteria / Forms / Standards","[DETAILS]"],["Reports / Deadlines","[DETAILS]"],["Authorized Data / Access","[DETAILS]"],["Conflicts / Recusal Process","[DETAILS]"],["Fee / Payment","[DETAILS]"],["Travel / Expenses","[DETAILS]"],["Materials / Ownership","[DETAILS]"],["Recording Permission","[DETAILS]"],["Credentials / Screening","[DETAILS]"],["Insurance","[DETAILS]"],["Term / Termination","[DETAILS]"],["Notices","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","EVALUATOR / TRAINER"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":419908,"sha256":"2c0691cfa3416990d3eb01aece078b794418ae3133059f71b70324782159c575"},{"key":"library-17-governmental-and-public-entity-services-agreement","code":"17","title":"GOVERNMENTAL AND PUBLIC ENTITY SERVICES AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"GOVERNMENTAL AND PUBLIC ENTITY SERVICES AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Public Entities","primaryUse":"Public schools, universities, municipalities, and government bodies.","filename":"17_Governmental_and_Public_Entity_Services_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/17_Governmental_and_Public_Entity_Services_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Governmental and Public Entity Services Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the identified governmental body, public school, district, state-supported institution, municipality, commission, authority, or other public entity for the services in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Scope; Authorization; No Work Before Approval","body":"RTBO shall perform only the authorized services in Schedule 1 after required purchase order, vendor registration, funding certification, contract review, board or governing-body approval, and execution. No employee’s request or course of dealing binds Public Entity beyond lawful authority."},{"title":"Compensation and Maximum Liability","body":"Rates, reimbursable expenses, invoice requirements, and not-to-exceed amount are stated in Schedule 1. Public Entity’s maximum payment obligation is limited to lawfully appropriated and available funds and the authorized contract amount. RTBO shall not perform excess work without a valid written amendment and required approvals."},{"title":"Procurement, Ethics, and Conflicts","body":"Each party shall comply with applicable procurement, lobbying, gratuity, nepotism, conflict, disclosure, debarment, sanctions, equal-opportunity, and ethics requirements. RTBO shall disclose actual or potential conflicts and certify required vendor eligibility. No contingent fee or improper benefit is authorized."},{"title":"Public Records and Confidential Information","body":"RTBO acknowledges that the agreement and related records may be subject to public disclosure. RTBO shall clearly mark claimed confidential material and provide the legal basis, but Public Entity determines disclosure obligations. Public Entity will provide notice when lawful and reasonably practicable, but is not liable for disclosure required by law."},{"title":"Audit, Records, and Access","body":"RTBO shall maintain complete books and supporting records for the legally required period and permit lawful inspection by Public Entity, legislative auditors, grantors, and authorized regulators. Access shall be limited to relevant records and conducted to protect unrelated confidential information where law permits."},{"title":"Nondiscrimination and Accessibility","body":"RTBO shall comply with applicable civil-rights, disability-access, equal-employment, and program-access requirements and shall provide reasonable cooperation concerning accommodations within its service responsibility. Public Entity shall provide facility and institutional accommodations under its control."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Insurance and Evidence of Coverage","body":"Each party shall maintain insurance reasonably appropriate to its obligations and risks, including commercial general liability, automobile liability when vehicles are used, workers’ compensation and employer’s liability when legally required, and professional, cyber, participant-accident, abuse/molestation, or umbrella coverage when the services create those exposures. Required limits, additional-insured status, primary/noncontributory wording, waivers of subrogation, and certificates shall be stated in Schedule 1. Insurance does not limit contractual liability."},{"title":"Governmental Limitations; No Waiver","body":"Nothing requires a public entity to indemnify, defend, insure, pay, or assume liability beyond authority granted by law or available appropriations, and nothing waives constitutional, statutory, sovereign, governmental, qualified, or other immunity. Any indemnity or liability obligation imposed on a public entity applies only to the extent lawfully authorized."},{"title":"Appropriation; Procurement; Audit; Public Records","body":"Payment obligations of a public entity are subject to lawful appropriation and available funds. The parties shall complete applicable bidding, purchasing, vendor-registration, conflict-disclosure, contract-review, and approval procedures. Records shall be maintained and made available for lawful audit. Materials may be subject to freedom-of-information or public-records laws; the receiving public entity will determine disclosure duties and, when legally permitted, provide notice before disclosing material marked confidential."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. This form preserves procurement, appropriation, audit, public-records, ethics, and immunity requirements but cannot determine the specific entity’s authority. The public entity’s counsel, procurement official, and authorized governing body must approve it before execution.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Public Entity","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Public Entity / Department","[LEGAL NAME]"],["Authority / Procurement Method","[STATUTE, SOLICITATION, COOPERATIVE CONTRACT, EXEMPTION]"],["Purchase Order / Contract Number","[NUMBER]"],["Services / Deliverables","[DETAILS]"],["Term","[DATES]"],["Rates / Expenses","[DETAILS]"],["Not-to-Exceed Amount","[AMOUNT]"],["Appropriation / Funding Source","[DETAILS]"],["Invoice / Payment Process","[DETAILS]"],["Required Certifications","[DEBARMENT, EEO, TAX, ETC.]"],["Insurance","[DETAILS]"],["Student / Personal Data","[DETAILS]"],["Public Records Contact","[DETAILS]"],["Contract Administrators","[DETAILS]"],["Approvals","[LEGAL, PROCUREMENT, BOARD, OTHER]"],["Special Terms","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","PUBLIC ENTITY"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Title: [TITLE]"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":47,"fileSize":420079,"sha256":"c73b2f56852252ad88f9fb037839bf56f09751467b6772fe641c561c11a1ddbd"},{"key":"library-18-participant-enrollment-assumption-of-risk-and-medical-authorization","code":"18","title":"PARTICIPANT ENROLLMENT, ASSUMPTION OF RISK, AND MEDICAL AUTHORIZATION","documentTitle":"PARTICIPANT ENROLLMENT, ASSUMPTION OF RISK, AND MEDICAL AUTHORIZATION","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Participants and Safety","primaryUse":"Participant and parent/guardian enrollment and emergency authorization.","filename":"18_Participant_Enrollment_Assumption_of_Risk_and_Medical_Authorization.docx","url":"library/docx/18_Participant_Enrollment_Assumption_of_Risk_and_Medical_Authorization.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Participant Enrollment, Assumption of Risk, and Medical Authorization is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the participant and, when the participant is a minor, the parent or legal guardian signing below for the program identified in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Enrollment and Eligibility","body":"Participant requests enrollment in the identified officiating, athletic, educational, classroom, video, evaluation, travel, or live-game activity and represents that submitted identity, age, medical, emergency, eligibility, and contact information is accurate. Participation is conditioned on payment, required forms, conduct, safety, and program rules."},{"title":"Activity Risks","body":"Participant understands that activities may include running, jumping, rapid direction changes, whistles and noise, crowded courts, balls and equipment, contact or collisions, falls, heat, weather, travel, communicable illness, emotional stress, live competition, and interaction with athletes, coaches, spectators, officials, and facilities. Risks include property loss, illness, concussion, musculoskeletal injury, disability, and, in rare cases, death."},{"title":"Voluntary Participation and Assumption of Inherent Risk","body":"Participant voluntarily chooses to participate with knowledge of the disclosed inherent and ordinary risks and assumes those risks to the extent permitted by law. Nothing in this form releases claims that cannot legally be released or excuses willful, reckless, grossly negligent, or unlawful conduct."},{"title":"Health, Fitness, and Accommodation","body":"Participant shall disclose information reasonably necessary for safe participation, follow medical restrictions, bring required medication or equipment, and stop and report symptoms or injury. RTBO is not providing medical advice. Requests for reasonable accommodation should be made promptly so the parties can engage in an appropriate process."},{"title":"Emergency Care Authorization","body":"If Participant is unable to consent and the emergency contact cannot be reached, Participant or Guardian authorizes reasonable first aid, emergency medical services, transportation, and treatment deemed necessary by qualified personnel. This authorization does not guarantee treatment and does not require RTBO personnel to exceed their training. Participant is responsible for treatment costs except as law or insurance provides otherwise."},{"title":"Conduct and Removal","body":"Participant shall follow safety, anti-harassment, safeguarding, academic-integrity, facility, technology, and instructor directions. RTBO may pause or remove Participant for safety, misconduct, ineligibility, nonpayment, or substantial disruption, subject to applicable refund policy and law. Retaliation for reporting a good-faith safety or misconduct concern is prohibited."},{"title":"Release and Responsibility to Extent Lawful","body":"To the extent permitted by applicable law, Participant releases RTBO and its directors, employees, contractors, instructors, and host partners from claims arising solely from inherent risks voluntarily assumed, but not from liabilities that law prohibits releasing. Participant is responsible for damage intentionally or negligently caused by Participant, subject to law."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Risk waivers and parent permissions vary by jurisdiction and may not waive negligence or minors’ claims. This form is designed for informed acknowledgment, conduct, emergency authorization, and risk allocation without purporting to waive rights that cannot lawfully be waived. Obtain local counsel review.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Participant / Parent or Guardian","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Program / Event","[NAME]"],["Dates / Times","[DETAILS]"],["Locations / Travel","[DETAILS]"],["Participant Name / DOB","[DETAILS]"],["Parent / Guardian, if minor","[DETAILS]"],["Emergency Contacts","[DETAILS]"],["Medical Conditions / Allergies / Medications","[DETAILS OR NONE]"],["Accommodation Request","[DETAILS OR NONE]"],["Insurance Information","[OPTIONAL / REQUIRED DETAILS]"],["Program Fee / Refund Policy","[DETAILS]"],["Transportation / Lodging","[DETAILS OR NOT INCLUDED]"],["Code of Conduct Incorporated","[DOCUMENT / LINK / DATE]"],["Media Choice","[SEPARATE RELEASE / DECLINED]"],["Special Restrictions","[DETAILS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","PARTICIPANT / PARENT OR GUARDIAN"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":45,"fileSize":419998,"sha256":"d64d3e6b229e8d914c83ab96850abb1579c3450a1fd359f5b00159b0aca85709"},{"key":"library-19-media-recording-and-publicity-release","code":"19","title":"MEDIA RECORDING AND PUBLICITY RELEASE","documentTitle":"MEDIA RECORDING AND PUBLICITY RELEASE","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Media and Publicity","primaryUse":"Choice-based image, video, audio, and publicity permission.","filename":"19_Media_Recording_and_Publicity_Release.docx","url":"library/docx/19_Media_Recording_and_Publicity_Release.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Media Recording and Publicity Release is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and the individual identified below and addresses photos, video, audio, interviews, name, likeness, voice, and submitted media for the specific uses selected in Schedule 1.","clauses":[{"title":"Grant of Permission","body":"Grantor authorizes RTBO to capture or use only the media types, identity elements, purposes, channels, territory, and period selected in Schedule 1. Permission includes reasonable editing, formatting, captions, cropping, accessibility adaptations, and combination with other material, but not materially deceptive alteration or an endorsement not authorized below."},{"title":"Ownership and License","body":"RTBO owns recordings it creates, subject to Grantor’s rights in name and likeness, and receives a nonexclusive license to submitted materials for the approved purposes. No transfer of Grantor’s underlying publicity rights is intended beyond this release."},{"title":"Compensation and Approval","body":"Compensation, if any, is stated in Schedule 1. Unless an approval right is expressly granted, Grantor waives inspection of final materials, but RTBO shall honor the selected scope and any legally effective revocation for future use. Previously printed or distributed materials and archival records may remain in circulation where withdrawal is impracticable."},{"title":"Privacy and Sensitive Contexts","body":"RTBO shall not intentionally publish private medical, education, background-screening, payment, or disciplinary information through this release. Names of minors, school affiliation, geolocation, testimonials, and close-up imagery shall be handled according to the selections and institutional requirements."},{"title":"No Misleading Endorsement","body":"This release does not authorize a statement that Grantor endorses a product, political position, sponsor, or service unless Schedule 1 expressly authorizes that endorsement and required advertising disclosures are made."},{"title":"Revocation and Takedown Requests","body":"Grantor may submit a written request to stop new uses. RTBO will take commercially reasonable steps for future controlled publications but cannot guarantee removal from third-party sharing, news reporting, cached systems, lawful archives, or materials already produced. A legally required withdrawal will be honored."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Indemnification","body":"To the fullest extent permitted by law, each party shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the other party and its directors, officers, employees, and agents from third-party claims, damages, judgments, penalties, and reasonable attorneys’ fees to the extent caused by the indemnifying party’s negligence, willful misconduct, breach of this Agreement, infringement, or violation of law. An indemnified party shall give prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and control of the defense, subject to consent before any settlement admitting fault or imposing nonmonetary obligations."},{"title":"Limitation of Liability","body":"Except for payment obligations, bodily injury or death, property damage, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, confidentiality or data-security breach, infringement, indemnification, or liabilities that cannot legally be limited, neither party is liable for consequential, incidental, special, exemplary, or punitive damages. Any negotiated aggregate cap appears in Schedule 1; absent an entered cap, no contractual cap applies."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Suspension; Termination; Effect","body":"Either party may terminate for convenience on the notice period in Schedule 1. Either party may terminate for a material breach not cured within ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for illegality, fraud, violence, abuse or safeguarding concerns, loss of required license or insurance, insolvency, material data breach, or conduct creating a substantial safety or reputational risk. RTBO may suspend an assignment or access while investigating. Earned, undisputed amounts remain payable; property and Confidential Information must be returned or destroyed; and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive."},{"title":"Force Majeure; Cancellations","body":"Neither party is liable for delay or nonperformance caused by events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disaster, epidemic, labor disruption, governmental action, venue closure, utility or communications failure, transportation emergency, or governing-body cancellation. The affected party shall notify the other promptly and mitigate. Event-specific cancellation, postponement, rescheduling, travel, and minimum-fee terms are governed by Schedule 1."},{"title":"Dispute Resolution; Governing Law","body":"The parties shall first attempt good-faith executive negotiation, followed by nonbinding mediation in Pulaski County, Arkansas, unless prohibited for a public entity. Any action not resolved by mediation shall be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Pulaski County, Arkansas, and governed by Arkansas law without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory law of another jurisdiction controls when it cannot lawfully be waived. EACH PARTY KNOWINGLY WAIVES TRIAL BY JURY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Use a separate choice-based release, especially for minors and educational settings. Participation in required educational or officiating services should not be conditioned on optional promotional consent unless lawful and clearly disclosed.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Person Granting Permission","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Grantor Name / Age","[DETAILS]"],["Parent / Guardian, if minor","[DETAILS]"],["Program / Event","[DETAILS]"],["Media Types Authorized","[PHOTO / VIDEO / AUDIO / INTERVIEW / SUBMITTED CONTENT]"],["Uses Authorized","[INSTRUCTIONAL / INTERNAL / WEBSITE / SOCIAL / ADVERTISING / PRESS / ARCHIVE]"],["Identity Elements","[NAME / FIRST NAME / LIKENESS / VOICE / TESTIMONIAL / SCHOOL]"],["Minor Privacy Choices","[NO NAME / NO GEOLOCATION / OTHER]"],["Territory / Channels","[DETAILS]"],["Permission Period","[DETAILS]"],["Compensation","[NONE / DETAILS]"],["Endorsement Authorized","[NO / SPECIFIC AUTHORIZATION]"],["Special Restrictions","[DETAILS]"],["Revocation Contact","[EMAIL / ADDRESS]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","GRANTOR / PARENT OR GUARDIAN"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":39,"fileSize":419209,"sha256":"3069a00339bfef773ad79678f0c568963adfed182579c2605902d9faac1b8b7a"},{"key":"library-20-sports-official-employment-agreement","code":"20","title":"SPORTS OFFICIAL EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT","documentTitle":"SPORTS OFFICIAL EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT","subtitle":"Standalone Agreement Template","category":"Workforce and Contractors","primaryUse":"Use when facts or law require employee treatment.","filename":"20_Sports_Official_Employment_Agreement.docx","url":"library/docx/20_Sports_Official_Employment_Agreement.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"This Sports Official Employment Agreement is between Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. and Employee for sports-officiating and related duties when RTBO elects or is legally required to treat the relationship as employment.","clauses":[{"title":"Employment, Position, and At-Will Status","body":"RTBO employs Employee in the position stated in Schedule 1. Unless a signed collective-bargaining agreement or state-specific addendum states otherwise, employment is at will: either party may end employment at any time, with or without cause or advance notice, subject to law. No manager may alter at-will status except by a writing signed by RTBO’s authorized officer."},{"title":"Duties and Standards","body":"Employee shall perform assigned games, events, training, reports, meetings, travel, and related duties; follow lawful instructions, rules, mechanics, safety, conduct, anti-harassment, safeguarding, expense, timekeeping, and technology policies; maintain required credentials; and exercise impartial officiating judgment. RTBO may reasonably modify duties consistent with law."},{"title":"Scheduling and Attendance","body":"RTBO will communicate schedules and assignment procedures. Employee shall accurately report availability, respond by deadlines, attend accepted or mandatory work, and promptly report lateness or absence. Scheduling, call-in, predictive-scheduling, rest, travel-time, and reporting-pay requirements will be administered under applicable law and Schedule 1."},{"title":"Compensation and Timekeeping","body":"Employee will be paid the wage or game-rate method in Schedule 1, subject to minimum wage, overtime, salary-basis, reporting-time, spread-of-hours, travel-time, and other applicable requirements. Employee must record all work time accurately and may not work off the clock. RTBO will correct reported errors and will not retaliate for wage concerns."},{"title":"Expenses, Equipment, and Deductions","body":"RTBO will reimburse required business expenses and provide or reimburse tools, uniforms, travel, and equipment as required by law and Schedule 1. Payroll deductions will be made only when legally permitted and properly authorized. Employee shall return RTBO property at separation."},{"title":"Payroll, Taxes, Benefits, and Leave","body":"RTBO will withhold and remit payroll taxes and provide workers’ compensation and unemployment coverage as required. Eligibility for benefits and paid or unpaid leave is governed by applicable plans, policies, and law; this agreement does not guarantee benefits not identified in a controlling plan."},{"title":"Policies, Investigations, and Discipline","body":"Employee shall acknowledge the current handbook and policies, which are not contracts unless expressly stated. RTBO may investigate complaints and impose lawful corrective action. Nothing prohibits reporting suspected legal violations, discussing wages or working conditions as protected by law, cooperating with government agencies, or making mandatory safeguarding reports."},{"title":"Confidentiality and Protected Activity","body":"Employee shall protect legitimate confidential and personal information, but this obligation does not prohibit legally protected whistleblowing, concerted activity, reporting discrimination or harassment, communicating with counsel or government, responding to legal process, or disclosing information as otherwise protected by law."},{"title":"Compliance With Laws and Governing-Body Rules","body":"Each party shall comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws; tax, wage-hour, civil-rights, accessibility, safety, anti-harassment, anti-retaliation, and recordkeeping requirements; and the rules, policies, bylaws, and eligibility standards of the applicable athletic association, conference, league, school system, sanctioning body, or facility. No term requires conduct prohibited by law or governing-body rule."},{"title":"Athlete Safety; Abuse Prevention; Mandatory Reporting","body":"Personnel with access to minors shall satisfy applicable screening, training, supervision, travel, one-on-one interaction, and abuse-prevention requirements before access. Nothing in this Agreement restricts or delays a mandatory report to law enforcement, the Arkansas Child Abuse Hotline, a child-protection agency, or another authority. Reports must be made directly by the person legally required to report; internal notice is supplemental and never a substitute. Retaliation against a good-faith reporter is prohibited."},{"title":"Confidentiality; Privacy; Information Security","body":"Each recipient shall use Confidential Information only to perform this Agreement, restrict access to personnel with a need to know, and protect it using reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. Student education records may be accessed only when the educational agency has determined the recipient performs an institutional service, is under the agency’s direct control regarding use and maintenance, meets the agency’s legitimate-interest criteria, uses records only for the disclosed purpose, and does not redisclose them except as legally permitted. A party discovering unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure shall contain it, preserve evidence, and notify the data owner without unreasonable delay and, where feasible, within twenty-four (24) hours."},{"title":"Intellectual Property; Names and Marks","body":"Each party retains its pre-existing intellectual property, systems, content, marks, and know-how. No license is granted except the limited, revocable right reasonably necessary to perform this Agreement. Public use of the other party’s name, logo, likeness, testimonial, photos, audio, or video requires prior written approval unless expressly authorized in a signed schedule."},{"title":"Employment Rights and Remedies","body":"Nothing in this Agreement requires Employee to indemnify RTBO for ordinary employment duties, waives workers’ compensation or unemployment rights, releases accrued wage or discrimination claims, restricts protected concerted activity, or limits any nonwaivable remedy. Any separate dispute-resolution program must be reviewed, separately presented, and enforceable under the law of the state where Employee works."},{"title":"Records; Taxes; Audit Support","body":"Each party shall maintain accurate performance, assignment, payment, incident, credential, insurance, and tax records for at least five (5) years after final payment, or longer when law, grant, audit, litigation hold, governing-body rule, or Schedule 1 requires. Each party is responsible for taxes legally imposed on it and shall provide required tax forms and supporting documentation."},{"title":"Separation; Final Pay; Return of Property","body":"Employment may end as stated in Section 1 and applicable law. RTBO will provide final pay, benefits information, notices, and continuation rights as required in the state where Employee works. Employee shall return RTBO property and preserve confidential information. Provisions concerning accrued compensation, protected rights, records, intellectual property, and confidentiality survive only to the lawful extent."},{"title":"Applicable Employment Law","body":"The mandatory employment law of each state and locality where Employee performs work governs to the extent it cannot be waived. Any Arkansas governing-law or venue term applies only when lawful and may not deprive Employee of nonwaivable wage, leave, discrimination, workers’ compensation, unemployment, whistleblower, labor, or other protections."},{"title":"Notices","body":"Formal notices must be in writing and delivered by personal delivery, nationally recognized overnight courier, certified U.S. mail, or email with confirmation of receipt to the addresses in Schedule 1. Notice is effective on receipt, except a refusal or failed delivery caused by an unreported address change is deemed receipt."},{"title":"General Terms; Electronic Signatures","body":"This Agreement, including signed schedules and incorporated attachments, is the entire agreement on its subject and supersedes prior discussions. Amendments and waivers must be in a writing signed by authorized representatives. Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent, except to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all relevant assets that assumes the obligations. Invalid terms will be narrowed or severed while the remainder remains effective. No waiver is continuing. Headings are for convenience. Counterparts and electronic records and signatures are effective to the extent permitted by applicable law."}],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Employment law varies by state and locality. Complete wage, overtime, minimum-call, reimbursement, leave, benefits, scheduling, workers’ compensation, unemployment, payroll, handbook, and at-will provisions with employment counsel for every state where work occurs.","tables":[[["Effective Date","[MONTH DAY, YEAR]"],["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","[STATE OF FORMATION] corporation | [ADDRESS]"],["Employee","[LEGAL NAME] | [ENTITY TYPE/STATE] | [ADDRESS]"],["Agreement Term","[START DATE] through [END DATE], unless earlier terminated"]],[["Item","Agreed Terms"],["Position / Classification","[TITLE; NONEXEMPT/EXEMPT AFTER LEGAL REVIEW]"],["Primary Work State(s)","[STATE(S)]"],["Start Date","[DATE]"],["Compensation","[HOURLY / GAME RATE / SALARY; RATE]"],["Pay Period","[DETAILS]"],["Overtime / Minimum Call / Travel Time","[LEGAL RULES AND POLICY]"],["Schedule / Availability","[DETAILS]"],["Duties / Sports / Levels","[DETAILS]"],["Supervisor","[NAME / TITLE]"],["Work Locations / Travel","[DETAILS]"],["Expense / Equipment Reimbursement","[DETAILS]"],["Benefits / Leave","[PLAN / POLICY REFERENCES]"],["Credentials / Screening","[DETAILS]"],["Handbook / Policies","[VERSION / DATE]"],["Notices","[DETAILS]"],["State-Specific Addenda","[LIST]"]],[["Raising The Bar Officiating Inc.","EMPLOYEE"],["By: ______________________________","By: ______________________________"],["Name: [AUTHORIZED SIGNER]","Name: [NAME]"],["Title: [TITLE]","Capacity: Individual"],["Date: ____________________________","Date: ____________________________"],["Email: [EMAIL]","Email: [EMAIL]"],["Address: [ADDRESS]","Address: [ADDRESS]"]]],"paragraphCount":43,"fileSize":419379,"sha256":"09d4c45ca1f4d081795cf067d98a1e831a67c23762352ae080a2057cdc4a0633"},{"key":"library-21a-background-check-disclosure","code":"21A","title":"BACKGROUND CHECK DISCLOSURE","documentTitle":"BACKGROUND CHECK DISCLOSURE","subtitle":"Standalone Consumer Report Disclosure - Keep Separate From Other Documents","category":"Background Screening","primaryUse":"Separate disclosure, authorization, pre-adverse, and final adverse notices.","filename":"21A_FCRA_Standalone_Background_Check_Disclosure.docx","url":"library/docx/21A_FCRA_Standalone_Background_Check_Disclosure.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. may obtain a “consumer report” about you from a consumer reporting agency for employment, contractor-engagement, officiating, assignment, credentialing, volunteer, or other legally permissible screening purposes. A consumer report may include information about criminal history, identity, address history, driving history, licenses, credentials, education, employment, sanctions, and other background information permitted by law.\n\nRTBO may also obtain an “investigative consumer report,” in which information about character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living is obtained through personal interviews. You may request additional information about the nature and scope of any investigative consumer report within a reasonable period after receiving this disclosure.\n\nA consumer report or investigative consumer report may be obtained at any time during the application, engagement, assignment, volunteer service, or employment relationship, when permitted by law and covered by your authorization.\n\nState or Local Notices Attached (if applicable): [LIST]","clauses":[],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. This disclosure must remain clear, conspicuous, and in a document consisting solely of the disclosure, apart from limited identifying information. Do not add a liability release, certification, employment terms, or unrelated acknowledgments. Add state and local notices when required.","tables":[[["Printed Name","____________________________________________"],["Signature","____________________________________________"],["Date","____________________________________________"]]],"paragraphCount":7,"fileSize":415039,"sha256":"dad2e26c559fe551304548ee346e85d75b37d4303126eba166b86b2f9f1b4188"},{"key":"library-21b-background-check-authorization","code":"21B","title":"BACKGROUND CHECK AUTHORIZATION","documentTitle":"BACKGROUND CHECK AUTHORIZATION","subtitle":"Written Authorization for Consumer and Investigative Consumer Reports","category":"Background Screening","primaryUse":"Separate disclosure, authorization, pre-adverse, and final adverse notices.","filename":"21B_FCRA_Background_Check_Authorization.docx","url":"library/docx/21B_FCRA_Background_Check_Authorization.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"I authorize Raising The Bar Officiating Inc., its authorized agents, and the consumer reporting agency identified below to obtain consumer reports and, if stated, investigative consumer reports about me for legally permissible employment, contractor-engagement, officiating, assignment, credentialing, volunteer, or related screening purposes. I authorize appropriate persons, employers, schools, licensing bodies, courts, agencies, repositories, and other lawful sources to provide information to the consumer reporting agency, subject to applicable law.\n\nThis authorization remains effective during the relationship to the extent permitted by law. I may revoke it prospectively in writing, but revocation does not affect reports already requested or actions already taken. I understand that refusal to authorize may prevent RTBO from completing screening required for the role.","clauses":[],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Use with the separate disclosure. Insert the screening company’s exact legal name and contact information. Obtain any state-specific authorization, copy-request, or check-box language required where the individual lives or works.","tables":[[["Full Legal Name","[FIRST / MIDDLE / LAST / SUFFIX]"],["Other Names Used","[DETAILS OR NONE]"],["Current Address","[STREET / CITY / STATE / ZIP]"],["Prior Addresses","[AS REQUESTED BY SCREENING PROVIDER]"],["Date of Birth","[MM/DD/YYYY - PROVIDE DIRECTLY TO CRA WHEN POSSIBLE]"],["Last Four of SSN","[XXXX - PROVIDE SECURELY WHEN REQUIRED]"],["Driver License","[STATE / NUMBER - ONLY WHEN DRIVING REPORT AUTHORIZED]"],["Consumer Reporting Agency","[LEGAL NAME / ADDRESS / PHONE / WEBSITE]"],["Copy of Report Requested","[YES / NO, if applicable]"],["Printed Name","____________________________________________"],["Signature","____________________________________________"],["Date","____________________________________________"]]],"paragraphCount":5,"fileSize":415344,"sha256":"c16e36d5af950892601e9def83a667008f2452b06082f7f76120401f694d15f0"},{"key":"library-21c-pre-adverse-action-notice","code":"21C","title":"PRE-ADVERSE ACTION NOTICE","documentTitle":"PRE-ADVERSE ACTION NOTICE","subtitle":"Opportunity to Review and Respond Before a Final Decision","category":"Background Screening","primaryUse":"Separate disclosure, authorization, pre-adverse, and final adverse notices.","filename":"21C_FCRA_Pre_Adverse_Action_Notice.docx","url":"library/docx/21C_FCRA_Pre_Adverse_Action_Notice.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. is considering an adverse decision concerning the role or opportunity identified above based in whole or in part on information in a consumer report. No final decision has been made.\n\nEnclosed or attached are: (1) a copy of the consumer report relied upon; and (2) the current A Summary of Your Rights Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act. Please review the report. You may dispute inaccurate or incomplete information directly with the consumer reporting agency and may provide RTBO with corrections, context, evidence of rehabilitation, identity-theft information, or other information you want considered by the response deadline.\n\nThe consumer reporting agency did not make RTBO’s decision and cannot explain why RTBO is considering the action. RTBO will consider timely information and any process required by applicable fair-chance, employment, credentialing, or other law before making a final decision.","clauses":[],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Send this notice before taking adverse action based in whole or in part on a consumer report. Attach a complete copy of the report and the current “A Summary of Your Rights Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act.” Allow a reasonable response period and comply with stricter state or local individualized-assessment, notice, or timing rules.","tables":[[["Date","[DATE]"],["Recipient","[NAME AND ADDRESS/EMAIL]"],["Role / Assignment","[POSITION OR OPPORTUNITY]"],["Consumer Reporting Agency","[LEGAL NAME / ADDRESS / TOLL-FREE PHONE / WEBSITE]"],["Response Deadline","[DATE AND TIME]"],["RTBO Contact","[NAME / TITLE / EMAIL / PHONE]"]]],"paragraphCount":12,"fileSize":415255,"sha256":"cc8f7e9eb031b5d192c32e490c08e877e128e3b713489678e9d187d02e8c84bb"},{"key":"library-21d-final-adverse-action-notice","code":"21D","title":"FINAL ADVERSE ACTION NOTICE","documentTitle":"FINAL ADVERSE ACTION NOTICE","subtitle":"Notice After Completion of Required Pre-Adverse Process","category":"Background Screening","primaryUse":"Separate disclosure, authorization, pre-adverse, and final adverse notices.","filename":"21D_FCRA_Final_Adverse_Action_Notice.docx","url":"library/docx/21D_FCRA_Final_Adverse_Action_Notice.docx","isGuide":false,"preamble":"Raising The Bar Officiating Inc. has made the final decision identified above based in whole or in part on information in a consumer report, after providing the pre-adverse notice and considering timely information received.\n\nThe consumer reporting agency identified above did not make this decision and cannot provide the specific reasons for it. You have the right to dispute with the consumer reporting agency the accuracy or completeness of information in the report. You also have the right to obtain an additional free copy of your report from that agency if you request it within sixty (60) days after receiving this notice.\n\nThis notice does not limit any additional rights under state or local fair-chance, background-check, employment, credentialing, discrimination, privacy, or other law. Questions about RTBO’s decision or any available review process should be directed to the RTBO contact above.","clauses":[],"useNotice":"IMPORTANT USE NOTICE. Send only after the pre-adverse process and any required waiting period, individualized assessment, or response review. Confirm that the decision is lawful, consistent, documented, and made by an authorized RTBO decision maker.","tables":[[["Date","[DATE]"],["Recipient","[NAME AND ADDRESS/EMAIL]"],["Role / Assignment","[POSITION OR OPPORTUNITY]"],["Decision","[DENIAL / WITHDRAWAL / SUSPENSION / OTHER]"],["Effective Date","[DATE]"],["Consumer Reporting Agency","[LEGAL NAME / ADDRESS / TOLL-FREE PHONE / WEBSITE]"],["RTBO Contact","[NAME / TITLE / EMAIL / PHONE]"]]],"paragraphCount":6,"fileSize":415133,"sha256":"985d57825ccbc0172c7bb912a043740cbda1cd4ba83354967c6caf9b4bf7f33d"}]};
